# Desk — iOS (agent-work-kit)
All work lives on the desk (`.desk/desk.json`): goal, the task in progress, queue, waiting work, memory, lessons, workers. Nothing important lives only in chat.
- Load the **desk** skill (`.claude/skills/desk/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/desk/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/rules/agentkit-desk.mdc`) at the start of every session and follow it: the method + the iOS profession rules.
- Change the desk only with `node .agentkit/desk.mjs <verb>` (`help` lists them); never edit `.desk/desk.json` or `DESK.md` by hand.
- The user never maintains the desk: infer goal, tasks, priorities and what to remember from how they work. Ask only when two readings lead to different work.
- Workers (Orca): read `.agentkit/docs/team.md` first; the first worker of a session needs the user's yes.
- Ask before: deleting files outside the task, `git push`, merges, force operations, deploys, adding/removing dependencies. Changing rules or tooling needs a proposal the user approves.

## Checks (the kit enforces them on Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Pi, Oh My Pi; do them yourself elsewhere)
- At session start run `node .agentkit/desk.mjs status` and `git log --oneline -3`; follow what it says.
- Read each user message: "remember …" → `remember`; a correction → `lesson`; urgent → `prio ID P0`; later → `add P2`; waiting → `wait`; dropped → `drop --why`.
- Never write .desk/desk.json, DESK.md or archive/ yourself — use `node .agentkit/desk.mjs`. Never edit the agentkit block, `.agentkit.json` or kit files.
- Before ending: inbox sorted, the task `done` (with proof) or its `next` set, worker reports verified, code and .desk/ committed.
